            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note" value="Where data is stored. Typed text sits in the form input until Add note. The blank-input check trims it. An accepted note is one string in the notes array, in this tab&#39;s JavaScript memory. index.html on disk is not changed.&#xa;&#xa;Reload. The browser discards the notes array with the page. The list starts empty. Closing the tab stops the app.&#xa;&#xa;Untrusted input. The note is data from the user, not code. The blank-input check is the gate: an empty or all-space value is rejected and the list does not change. Accepted text is stored as a string and shown with textContent, so the browser displays the characters and does not interpret them as HTML. That is the boundary between untrusted input and the code that handles it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff8e7;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=10;fontSize=14;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#1f2933;" vertex="1" parent="1">
